     "design": {
      "purpose": "Read a tally chart with three groups: how many in one group, how many more, and how many in all.",
      "principles": [
       "PRINCIPLE_MULTIPLE_REPRESENTATIONS"
      ],
      "rationale": "Tally marks are drawn in groups of five, four strokes crossed by a fifth, so students can count by fives and then ones. The three questions ask for a count, a comparison and a total, which are the questions grade 1 asks of data with up to three categories.",
      "misconceptions": [
       "Counts a group of five as four, missing the crossing stroke.",
       "Answers how many more with the larger count instead of the difference."
      ],
